SUMMARY:FORBIDDEN: Chaos By Design US Tour 2026
DESCRIPTION:Sunday November 8th\, 2026\nDoors | 6:00 PM\nShow | 6:30 PM \nGeneral Admission Standing Room | $34.70 + Fees\nReserved Balcony & Mezzanine Seating | $45.40 + Fees \nPlease note\, there is a strict 8 ticket limit for this event. Accounts found in violation of the posted ticket limit may be cancelled without notice.\n+$5 on All Day of Show Purchases\nThis event is all ages – 21+ With Valid ID to Drink\nCome hungry! Snacks and light bites will be available at the canteen.\n—————————————————\nPresented by Big Fan Presents\n—————————————————\nFORBIDDEN Chaos By Design US Tour 2026 \nGodfathers in the Bay Area metal scene\, Forbidden have returned with their first album in 16 years to unleash 12 fierce\, uncompromising\, and supremely progressive songs which signal an almighty return. Forbidden will be released by BLKIIBLK Records and charts a defiant journey through scything riffs\, incredible melodies\, 24 karat lead guitars\, simply thunderous drums and bass\, plus the studio debut of Norman Skinner (Niviane & Imagika) whose soaring vocals elevate the material to unprecedented levels.  \nConceived by founder and guitarist Craig Locicero alongside his creative brother\, drummer Chris Kontos\, the foundational energy of bassist Matt Camacho\, the versatility and poise of guitarist Jeremy Von Epp\, and Skinner’s voracious fresh approach\, Forbidden sees the band arriving at their finest hour with their richest-ever line-up. With Skinner stepping up to take  on lyrical duties\, Forbidden takes a fierce and uncompromising look into the eyes of our times without taking sides\, instead imploring people to recognize the false conflicts created by the current society and how they can conquer and rise above them.  \nTake the blistering roar of “Single Point Failure”\, the beautiful orchestral savagery of “Flower of Life”\, and the relentless charge of “Burning The Lungs Of Earth.” There’s also the mid-paced brooding power of “Psyclops\,” the twisting\, winding power force of “Sycophantasy” featuring guest vocals from Mastodon’s Brann Dailor\, and a thunderous ode to women “The Burden” featuring guest vocals from Kayla Dixon. In addition\, Forbidden pay homage to classic American heavy metal band\, Savatage in the shape of a malevolent and mesmeric cover of “Sirens”\, which embraces Greek mythology.  \nRecorded\, produced and engineered at Sharkbite Studios in Oakland\, California with engineer and co-producer Zack Ohren\, Forbidden is the the resounding realization of a band which has finally found inner-peace\, and furious cohesion\, in expressing its true passionate angst and incredible metal heart. \nCheck out Forbidden here!\nWebsite | Instagram | Facebook \nSupported By: Heathen\, Void & Divination\n—————————————————\n*Ticket Alert*  \nTickets for Mickey’s Black Box are sold through TicketMaster\, via our website\, or in person at our Box Office. Any tickets purchased elsewhere will not be honored and we are not responsible for tickets purchased from any 3rd party sellers.  Do not google the name of the band to search for tickets.  Go to Mickeysblackbox.com ONLY. Mickeysblackbox.com will never direct you anywhere but the official TicketMaster event site. \n\nAll bags are subject are to search upon entry. Tickets are non-refundable\, save for instances in which performances are cancelled by Mickey’s Black Box. For more information about our venue or to make an ADA request\, please visit the FAQ page of our website: https://mickeysblackbox.com/faq/ or call our box office line at (717) 723 – 8463.
URL:https://mickeysblackbox.com/event/forbidden-chaos-by-design-us-tour-2026/
LOCATION:Mickey’s Black Box\, 101 Rock Lititz Boulevard\, Lititz\, PA\, 17543\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://mickeysblackbox.com/app/uploads/2026/07/Untitled-July-20-2026-at-18.04.02-scaled.jpeg
END:VEVENT
